 explain what is meant by a ‘highly concentrated’ market for potato crisps (Extract A, lines 2–3).","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["concentrated market","concentration ratio","oligopoly","crisps"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":4,"ctxPage":3,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2019-jun-q1c","p":18,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(c)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"In Extract A, lines 15–16, it was suggested that some firms may respond to the advertising ban by cutting the prices of their products. Using game theory and the information provided in Figure 1 and Extract A, discuss the effects on firms of cutting prices in an oligopolistic market.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["game theory","price war","oligopoly","interdependence"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":6,"ctxPage":3,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2018-jun-q1b","p":17,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(b)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 3 and other information provided, discuss the price and non-price strategies that Starbucks may use to increase profitability.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly","3-3-1-revenue"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["price strategies","non-price competition","Starbucks","profitability"],"qpPage":6,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":4,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2017-jun-q6a","p":0,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(a)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"With reference to Figure 1 and Extract A, explain one likely reason for the change in the four-firm concentration ratio of the supermarket sector between 2010 and 2015.","topics":["3-4-4-oligopoly"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["concentration ratio","supermarkets","oligopoly","market share"],"qpPage":15,"msPage":10,"ctxPage":13,"modelAnswer":null}]}
